Scripts in this directory. "Load-bearing" means the Makefile or CI calls it.

run-all.sh          load-bearing  'make test' and CI. Compiles and runs every
                                  stress-tests/**/*.cpp (skipping helpers/,
                                  gen.cpp and *brute.cpp) with g++ -std=c++17
                                  -O2 and stdin closed, using a precompiled
                                  stress-tests/utilities/template.h. Any
                                  nonzero exit is a failed test.
compile-all.sh      load-bearing  'make test-compiles' and CI. Syntax-checks
                                  every content/**/*.h except the ones listed
                                  in skip_headers.
test-compiles.sh    load-bearing  one header, called by compile-all.sh: writes
                                  build/temp.cpp = template.cpp + the header
                                  and compiles that. Run from the repo root.
skip_headers        load-bearing  data, not a script: the headers that cannot
                                  compile on their own, one path per line,
                                  matched as a fixed substring (grep -F), '#'
                                  comments allowed. Each entry says why.
spacing.py          occasional    formatter for the spacing conventions
                                  (spaces around operators, after commas,
                                  ') {', casts). Dry run by default, --apply
                                  writes; it asserts the whitespace-stripped
                                  md5 is unchanged, so it can never alter code.
find-unreferenced-files.py
                    report        prints content/**/*.h that the chapter.tex
                                  next to them does not name. 'make
                                  showexcluded' is the better version -- it
                                  covers .py/.java too and understands
                                  \kactlimport[opts]{file}.
add-cc0-license.py  historical    one-off: inserted "License: CC0" into the
                                  files listed in a './todo' file.
fix-newlines.py     historical    one-off: normalised the blank lines around
                                  '#pragma once'.
